fe's name they tell us telus became a  suspect early on due to those public  comments he had made about german in his  reporting back out here live sheriff joe  lombardo making a rare public appearance  because of this high profile case they  put so many resources in solving this in  solving this homicide quickly we will  tell you what the sheriff said and also  bring you some new details coming up  this afternoon live at four o'clock for  now i'm david charns live outside metro  my colleague victoria saha is live  outside the regional justice center  where robert telus is expected to be in  court at 1 30 this afternoon victoria  what are you learning  hey there david thank you yep robert  telus will be facing the judge for the  first time since being charged with the  murder of jeff german and it was an  intense situation that led up to his  arrest starting from yesterday morning  up until late last night as police tried  to take custody and charge telus  ultimately it was dna evidence that led  police to their suspect  ever since jeff gearman was found  stabbed to death outside his home  saturday morning police have been urging  for the public's help to find his killer  after releasing new video of the suspect  and a potential car earlier in the week  by wednesday telus was the prime suspect  wednesday morning police issued a search  warrant at telus house questioning him  at metro and they confiscated potential  evidence including his car and clothing  hours later telus returned home in a  white jumpsuit and refused to comment  then as police were trying to contact  him there was no answer at the door  sources tell our 8 news now  investigators telus was taken into  custody after he was taken to the  hospital with non-life-threatening  self-inflicted wounds our 8 news now  cameras were there as he was wheeled in  now for the first time we are hearing  from  gearman's family they sent in a  statement to eight news now saying in  part we're shocked we're saddened and  angry about his death jeff was committed  to seeking justice for others and would  appreciate the hard work by local police  again robert tellis will be in court in  just over an hour he's facing an open  murder charge i'm going to go ahead and  send it over to my colleague candace is  outside the public administrator's  office candace has there been any new  developments  very good after folks well the  building where robert tell us work is  still closed and i've spoken to some of  the people who are running for his  position now and they tell me that this  all comes as a shock of course the  public administration building was  searched by police wednesday morning  employees were told to go home wednesday  afternoon and it's been closed ever  since i reached out to the city official  who beat tell us in the primaries for  the position read read her husband told  me her phone was confiscated during the  search reads on the november ballot with  tablet al debac and patsy brown for tell  us his position as public administrator  brown's campaign team told me this  incident has everyone including brown on  alert  the concern of personal safety  and i know that's something that a lot  of the employees of the public  administrator's office even the  candidates who are also  seeking office for public administrator  that's something that is going to  resonate and be at the forefront of  their mind  brown had a bit of controversy herself  she was recently arrested for a dui her  campaign team says she's been warning  her father and that she was set to meet  with german next week i reached out to  tabitha and didn't get a response but  the county sent this statement saying  quote the death of jeff german was both  shocking and tragic and we joined with  our community and being stunned at how  this situation has continued to evolve  over the last few days the public  administrator is an elected position and  the county is reviewing its options  under the law regarding robert telus's  current status as the public  administrator the safety of our county  employees and the public is our top  priority and the county has suspended mr  telus access to county offices or  property they say it is undetermined at  this time when this building will be  open of course we will keep you up to  date with stick with us right here for  the latest heather  all right candace thank you so much for  that report now gearman as we've  reported was a journalist here in las  vegas for nearly four decades on the las  vegas review journal executive editor  released a statement on the arrest and  here's what it reads in part  the arrest of robert tellis is at once  an enormous relief and an outrage for  the review journal newsroom we're  relieved that telus is in custody and  outraged that a colleague appears to  have been killed for reporting on an  elected official

